WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.718 --> 00:00:22.244
On Midsummer eve Adele, who was weary from gathering wild strawberries, went to bed with the sun.

2
00:00:23.465 --> 00:00:26.368
I watched her fall asleep, and then I headed for the orchard.

3
00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:31.112
No part of Thornfield was more sheltered and more Eden-like.

4
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:39.034
A winding path, bordered with laurel bushes, ended in a giant chestnut tree encircled by a wooden bench.

5
00:00:40.294 --> 00:00:44.575
As I walked along, I suddenly smelled a familiar scent: Mr.

6
00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:45.916
Rochester's cigar.

7
00:00:47.076 --> 00:00:52.698
I came around a bend in the path, and there he was, examining a large moth that had

8
00:00:52.738 --> 00:00:53.798
alighted on a plant.

9
00:00:54.958 --> 00:01:00.500
"He has his back toward me," I said to myself, "so if I walk softly, I can slip

10
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.957
away." But somehow he heard footsteps and knew they were mine.

11
00:01:04.977 --> 00:01:07.778
"Jane, come look at this fellow.

12
00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:10.498
Oh, there he goes!"

13
00:01:11.739 --> 00:01:15.720
The moth flew away, and I also retreated, but Mr.

14
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.880
Rochester followed me.

15
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.641
"Turn back, Jane.

16
00:01:20.781 --> 00:01:23.442
On so lovely a night, it's a shame to sit in the house."

17
00:01:24.702 --> 00:01:30.144
Sometimes my tongue is prompt with an answer, but there are times when it sadly fails me.

18
00:01:31.376 --> 00:01:34.158
At this late hour I didn't like to walk alone with Mr.

19
00:01:34.218 --> 00:01:38.640
Rochester in the shadowy orchard, but I couldn't find an excuse to leave him.

20
00:01:39.821 --> 00:01:41.982
We walked slowly toward the chestnut tree.

21
00:01:42.002 --> 00:01:45.684
"Thornfield is a pleasant place in summer, isn't it?"

22
00:01:46.024 --> 00:01:46.464
he said.

23
00:01:46.484 --> 00:01:48.165
"Yes, sir."

24
00:01:48.185 --> 00:01:54.329
"And, even though I don't understand it, I perceive that you have a degree of regard for that

25
00:01:54.449 --> 00:01:57.250
foolish Adele and even for simple Mrs.

26
00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.872
Fairfax." "Yes, sir.

27
00:02:01.116 --> 00:02:02.737
I would be sorry to part from them."

28
00:02:02.758 --> 00:02:05.360
"That's always the way life is."

29
00:02:06.561 --> 00:02:07.902
He sighed and paused.

30
00:02:07.922 --> 00:02:14.087
"No sooner have you settled in a pleasant place than a voice tells you to rise and move

31
00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.009
on." "Must I leave Thornfield?"

32
00:02:17.029 --> 00:02:21.512
"Yes, because in about a month I will marry Blanche Ingram.

33
00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:27.397
You said yourself that when this happens, Adele must go to school and you must leave."

34
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:29.179
"Yes, sir.

35
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:36.262
I hope I was going to say that I hoped I could remain until I found another position.

36
00:02:37.442 --> 00:02:40.624
But I stopped because my voice was not under control.

37
00:02:41.884 --> 00:02:43.365
Mr. Rochester continued.

38
00:02:43.385 --> 00:02:48.787
"Through my future mother-in-law I've already heard of a position that I think will suit you.

39
00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:54.790
Mrs. O'Gall of Connaught, Ireland, is in need of a governess for her five daughters.

40
00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:56.870
You'll like Ireland.

41
00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:00.292
I've heard that the people are so warmhearted there."

42
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.684
"It's a long way off, sir, and the sea is such a barrier from—" "From what, Jane?"

43
00:03:07.704 --> 00:03:13.027
"From England and Thornfield—and you, sir."

44
00:03:14.248 --> 00:03:15.829
Tears gushed from my eyes.

45
00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:19.111
We had reached the chestnut, and Mr.

46
00:03:19.171 --> 00:03:20.812
Rochester asked me to sit with him.

47
00:03:20.832 --> 00:03:24.614
"When you go to Ireland, I will never see you again.

48
00:03:25.775 --> 00:03:27.496
That is certain," he said.

49
00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:32.222
"I sometimes feel that the two of us are connected by an invisible string.

50
00:03:33.343 --> 00:03:36.845
But at that distance, I'm afraid the string will snap and you'll forget me."

51
00:03:36.865 --> 00:03:42.848
"I'll never—" I could not go on and sobbed convulsively.

52
00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:49.112
When I regained my composure, I said, "I wish I'd never been born or come to Thornfield."

53
00:03:49.132 --> 00:03:51.513
"Because you're sorry to leave it?"

54
00:03:52.674 --> 00:03:55.575
"Yes. And because I've known you, Mr.

55
00:03:55.635 --> 00:04:00.681
Rochester, it strikes me with terror and anguish that I must be torn from you forever.

56
00:04:02.662 --> 00:04:07.023
I see the necessity of leaving, and it's like looking on the necessity of death."

57
00:04:08.263 --> 00:04:09.644
"Where do you see the necessity?"

58
00:04:10.024 --> 00:04:10.564
he asked.

59
00:04:10.584 --> 00:04:13.625
"I tell you I must go!"

60
00:04:13.645 --> 00:04:15.105
I said passionately.

61
00:04:15.125 --> 00:04:18.626
"Do you think I can stay here to become nothing to you?

62
00:04:19.927 --> 00:04:21.847
I have a heart, and I can't ignore it!

63
00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:24.908
I speak to you now as if we are equals."

64
00:04:26.196 --> 00:04:27.217
"And so we are!"

65
00:04:27.637 --> 00:04:28.137
said Mr.

66
00:04:28.197 --> 00:04:31.338
Rochester, gathering me in his arms and kissing me.

67
00:04:31.358 --> 00:04:33.179
"Let me go!"

68
00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:35.340
I cried, struggling against him.

69
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.822
"You're as good as married to one whom I do not believe you truly love."

70
00:04:40.963 --> 00:04:43.804
I freed myself from his embrace and stood before him.

71
00:04:43.824 --> 00:04:50.727
"Jane, I offer you my hand, my heart, and a share of all my possessions.

72
00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:53.228
I summon you as my wife.

73
00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.443
You are the only one that I ever intended to marry."

74
00:04:59.405 --> 00:05:00.886
I thought he was mocking me.

75
00:05:00.906 --> 00:05:06.271
"Your bride, Miss Ingram, stands between us."

76
00:05:07.592 --> 00:05:11.715
He rose and with a stride reached me and drew me into his arms again.

77
00:05:11.735 --> 00:05:16.139
"My bride is here because my equal is here.

78
00:05:17.421 --> 00:05:19.062
Jane, will you marry me?"

79
00:05:19.082 --> 00:05:22.508
"But Miss Ingram Mr.

80
00:05:22.528 --> 00:05:27.630
Rochester explained that he did not love her and that she was only interested in his money.

81
00:05:28.831 --> 00:05:32.933
He caused a rumor to reach her that his fortune was just a third of what it was

82
00:05:32.993 --> 00:05:33.773
believed to be.

83
00:05:35.054 --> 00:05:38.735
After that both Blanche and her mother treated him coldly.

84
00:05:40.016 --> 00:05:43.517
I studied his face to satisfy myself that he was telling the truth.

85
00:05:43.537 --> 00:05:46.458
"Oh, Jane, accept my proposal!"

86
00:05:46.799 --> 00:05:47.339
he cried.

87
00:05:47.359 --> 00:05:49.800
"Tell me you will marry me."

88
00:05:51.148 --> 00:05:53.049
I still could not believe what I was hearing.

89
00:05:53.069 --> 00:05:55.350
"Do you truly love me?

90
00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.872
Do you sincerely wish me to be your wife?"

91
00:05:58.892 --> 00:06:01.274
"I do."

92
00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:05.116
"Then, dear Edward, I will marry you."

93
00:06:06.296 --> 00:06:11.319
We embraced, and again and again he said, "Are you happy, Jane?"

94
00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.521
And again and again I replied, "Yes."

95
00:06:16.982 --> 00:06:22.934
After which he murmured, "I found her poor and friendless, and I will love and cherish her.

96
00:06:24.155 --> 00:06:29.039
I know God sanctions what I do, and so I wash my hands of the world's judgment."

97
00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:33.583
The moon had not yet set, but we were in complete darkness.

98
00:06:34.844 --> 00:06:38.647
I could scarcely see my master's face, though I was very close to him.

99
00:06:39.908 --> 00:06:45.973
Suddenly the chestnut tree writhed and groaned, while wind roared in the laurel walk and came sweeping over

100
00:06:46.093 --> 00:06:50.353
us. "The weather is changing; we must go in," said Mr.

101
00:06:50.413 --> 00:06:55.637
Rochester. Before I could reply, there was a flash of lightning and a crash of thunder.

102
00:06:57.439 --> 00:06:58.880
The rain rushed down.

103
00:07:00.061 --> 00:07:04.385
He hurried me through the grounds and into the house, but we were quite wet by the time

104
00:07:04.425 --> 00:07:05.346
we reached the hall.

105
00:07:06.547 --> 00:07:07.888
The clock struck midnight.

106
00:07:07.908 --> 00:07:11.611
"Hasten to take off your wet things," he said.

107
00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.913
"Goodnight, my darling."

108
00:07:15.194 --> 00:07:16.616
He kissed me repeatedly.

109
00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.521
When I looked up, I saw Mrs.

110
00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:24.284
Fairfax standing there, looking pale, grave, and amazed.

111
00:07:25.605 --> 00:07:30.348
I smiled at her and ran upstairs, thinking that all could be explained to her tomorrow.

112
00:07:31.568 --> 00:07:35.731
I still felt a pang that she should even temporarily misconstrue what she had seen.

113
00:07:36.952 --> 00:07:39.994
But joy soon erased every other feeling.

114
00:07:41.334 --> 00:07:47.240
Before I left my bed the next morning, Adele came running in to report that the huge chestnut

115
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.305
tree in the orchard had been split in two by lightning.
